##Python Seat Booking System
A simple, interactive command-line Python script that dynamically generates a seating grid and allows users to reserve available seats.

🚀 Features
Dynamic Seat Generation: Automatically creates a list of available seats labeled from A1 to K10 (using ASCII character generation).

Interactive Booking: Runs an continuous loop prompting the user to input their desired seat.

Built-in Validation:

Prevents users from booking seats that don't exist (e.g., typing "Z99").

Prevents double-booking by checking if a seat is already in the reserved list.

Booking Summary: Displays a complete list of all successfully booked seats upon exiting the program.

🛠️ How to Use
Run the script in your Python environment.

When prompted with enter you seat :, type the seat you want to book (e.g., A1, C5, K10).

If the seat is available, you will see a success message. If it is invalid or taken, you will receive an error warning.

To exit the program and view your final booking summary, simply type no.

💻 Code Overview
The script utilizes standard Python features including:

for loops and range() for grid generation.

chr() to convert integer values to ASCII letters.

while True loops for continuous user input.

try...except blocks with ValueError for clean error handling.
